@startuml
' ADAS Camera HIL Testing Platform Block Diagram
title ADAS Camera HIL Testing Platform
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF7CC
skinparam noteBorderColor #AA8C00
left to right direction

actor "ADAS Test Engineer" as Engineer
actor "Data Annotation Specialist" as Annotator

rectangle "Data Management & Ground Truth" as DM {
  rectangle "Video Ingestion\n(Upload, decode, catalog)" as VI
  rectangle "Automated Annotation\n(AI bounding boxes + IDs)" as AA
  rectangle "Annotation Validation & Editing UI" as AV
  database "Video & Ground Truth Library" as VL
}

rectangle "Test Configuration" as TC {
  rectangle "Project Workspace\n(Project builder & playlist)" as PW
}

rectangle "Test Execution" as TE {
  rectangle "HIL Test Control UI\n(Session setup, LabJack status)" as HTC
  rectangle "Playback & Sync Engine\n(Time 0 reference, expected events)" as PSE
  rectangle "LabJack DAQ Interface\n(Signal capture, timestamps)" as LJ
}

rectangle "Analysis & Reporting" as AR {
  rectangle "Performance Analyzer\n(Latency + detection outcomes)" as PA
  rectangle "Report Generator\n(Summaries + failure snapshots)" as RG
}

Engineer --> VI : Upload footage
Engineer --> PW : Build project playlists
Engineer --> HTC : Launch HIL test run
Engineer <-- RG : Review reports
Annotator --> AV : Validate annotations

VI --> AA : Processed videos
AA --> AV : Pre-annotated footage
AV --> VL : Validated ground truth
VL --> PW : Select validated videos
PW --> HTC : Playlist + latency threshold
HTC --> PSE : Start playback session
PSE --> LJ : Detection trigger expectations
LJ --> PSE : Signal events + timestamps
PSE --> PA : Expected event timeline
LJ --> PA : Hardware signal log
PA --> RG : Pass/fail + latency metrics
RG --> VL : Failure snapshots metadata

note top of PSE
  Uses monotonic clock for sub-ms
timestamp alignment
end note

note right of LJ
  Interfaces with LabJack T7
  Digital high/low capture
end note

note bottom of RG
  Generates package of summary stats
  and image excerpts for failures
end note

@enduml
